    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] It opened at the Opera Comique in London, on 25 May 1878 and ran for 571 performances, which was the second-longest run of any musical theatre piece up to that time.\n[2] Associated with the Paris theatre of the same name, \"opéra comique\" is not always comic or light in nature; \"Carmen\", perhaps the most famous \"opéra comique\", is a tragedy.\n[3] It was first performed on 9 February 1878 at the Opera Comique by the Comedy Opera Company as a companion piece to \"The Sorcerer\".\n[4] The libretto was written by Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy, based on a novella of the same title by Prosper Mérimée."
